1
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:18,500
Did you sleep well?

2
00:00:20,066 --> 00:00:21,300
Yeah.

3
00:00:22,333 --> 00:00:25,500
I haven't slept this well in a long time.

4
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,133
Really?

5
00:00:33,766 --> 00:00:35,000
Yeah.

6
00:00:36,933 --> 00:00:38,433
You're so cute.

7
00:00:44,866 --> 00:00:47,500
But you're cuter.

8
00:00:52,733 --> 00:00:54,600
Claire, stop teasing.

9
00:01:55,866 --> 00:01:57,200
What are you doing?

10
00:02:00,666 --> 00:02:03,000
Can I get a hug?

11
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:07,500
Sure, but I smell like food.

12
00:02:08,600 --> 00:02:09,700
Let me smell.

13
00:02:11,333 --> 00:02:12,600
You don't smell bad at all.

14
00:02:12,933 --> 00:02:14,000
I do.

15
00:02:14,366 --> 00:02:16,233
Smells amazing to me.

16
00:02:19,733 --> 00:02:21,133
It stinks.

17
00:02:21,133 --> 00:02:22,500
Can't you see I'm cooking?

18
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:24,200
I smell like sausages all over.

19
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:26,800
Can I have a taste?

20
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:36,600
Hold on a sec.

21
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:44,000
Yes, Chief Ed.

22
00:02:46,966 --> 00:02:49,366
Yes, you'll definitely have it by tomorrow.

23
00:02:50,766 --> 00:02:51,766
Got it.

24
00:02:58,733 --> 00:03:00,766
My editor called for the draft again.

25
00:03:03,666 --> 00:03:05,966
But I still have no idea about an ending.

26
00:03:09,066 --> 00:03:10,800
You can do this, fighting!

27
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:14,000
Cher also messaged me to hurry up.

28
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,233
Once I'm done, I'll come straight to you.

29
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:38,433
I'm sorry, Claire.

30
00:03:38,433 --> 00:03:40,833
But this novel has to be absolutely perfect.

31
00:04:36,166 --> 00:04:39,200
The tears streaming down his cheeks...

32
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:43,566
Are the sweetest taste of failure.

33
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Such a profound description, Ms. Writer.

34
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:12,200
This is crazy, so crazy!

35
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:13,900
I can't take this.

36
00:05:13,900 --> 00:05:15,500
It's just too much.

37
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:18,200
What are you rambling about?

38
00:05:19,200 --> 00:05:21,233
I just feel so bad for her.

39
00:05:22,400 --> 00:05:23,500
Feel bad for who?

40
00:05:24,533 --> 00:05:26,000
For Warin, of course.

41
00:05:27,766 --> 00:05:30,033
Is that your ex? Doesn't sound familiar.

42
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:34,000
Hey, are you crazy? This Warin.

43
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,100
This! This Warin right here!

44
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:41,000
The male lead in this novel.

45
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:41,533
Look.

46
00:05:43,266 --> 00:05:45,500
Why? Did the male lead die?

47
00:05:45,866 --> 00:05:47,600
Did she find someone new?

48
00:05:47,600 --> 00:05:50,266
Ugh, no! Listen to me.

49
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:53,533
The male lead didn't want love.

50
00:05:53,533 --> 00:05:55,500
Because of his past family trauma.

51
00:05:56,100 --> 00:05:58,500
But he finally opened up to her.

52
00:06:01,133 --> 00:06:02,166
Oh, really?

53
00:06:03,066 --> 00:06:04,200
Yeah.

54
00:06:05,100 --> 00:06:06,500
Then what happened?

55
00:06:08,166 --> 00:06:08,733
Look.

56
00:06:09,266 --> 00:06:12,533
"The tears streaming down his cheeks...

57
00:06:12,533 --> 00:06:15,366
...are the sweetest taste of failure."

58
00:06:16,566 --> 00:06:18,566
How did Eris even come up with this?

59
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,633
We're her fans for a reason.

60
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:28,866
But now that I think about it...

61
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,800
The plot sounds a lot like your story.

62
00:06:38,166 --> 00:06:39,300
I wonder...

63
00:06:40,766 --> 00:06:44,266
Maybe my life is just a generic plot.

64
00:06:46,800 --> 00:06:49,700
So people just easily use it for drama.

65
00:07:04,566 --> 00:07:06,000
Hello there.

66
00:07:06,766 --> 00:07:07,633
Ms. Eris!

67
00:07:08,233 --> 00:07:09,733
Perfect timing!

68
00:07:09,733 --> 00:07:11,766
I'm reading your new novel right now.

69
00:07:13,133 --> 00:07:16,500
How did you come up with this line?

70
00:07:17,133 --> 00:07:20,166
"The tears streaming down his cheeks...

71
00:07:20,166 --> 00:07:22,633
...are the sweetest taste of failure."

72
00:07:28,166 --> 00:07:29,800
Cher.

73
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,466
Ms. Eris...

74
00:07:32,133 --> 00:07:34,800
is a famous novelist.

75
00:07:38,266 --> 00:07:42,500
She knows exactly what to write to get people hooked.

76
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:47,000
Claire, please listen to me first.

77
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:55,500
Are you here to celebrate your views?

78
00:07:56,700 --> 00:07:59,200
Or are you just here for more data?

79
00:08:02,266 --> 00:08:03,700
When you wrote about

80
00:08:03,700 --> 00:08:06,833
"the sweetest taste of failure"

81
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:10,300
Did you mean how I feel being used?

82
00:08:10,300 --> 00:08:12,433
Or the money piling up in your account

83
00:08:12,433 --> 00:08:14,333
because you sold my secrets for cash?

84
00:08:17,566 --> 00:08:18,500
Well...

85
00:08:19,766 --> 00:08:23,666
I gotta take Charcoal out for a walk.

86
00:08:24,266 --> 00:08:25,400
I must excuse myself.

87
00:08:32,100 --> 00:08:32,733
You know what

88
00:08:34,433 --> 00:08:36,333
What makes me the angriest

89
00:08:36,333 --> 00:08:38,200
is not that you wrote about me,

90
00:08:44,866 --> 00:08:47,233
"The tears streaming down his cheeks...

91
00:08:48,966 --> 00:08:52,400
...are the sweetest taste of failure."

92
00:08:59,666 --> 00:09:02,133
Such a profound description, Ms. Writer.

93
00:09:03,300 --> 00:09:05,800
Plus, the plot matches our story perfectly.

94
00:09:06,400 --> 00:09:08,600
Claire, please don't misunderstand.

95
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:11,100
It's just a plot in a novel.

96
00:09:11,100 --> 00:09:14,533
Other writers also draw inspiration from their surroundings.

97
00:09:14,800 --> 00:09:16,166
Inspiration?

98
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:19,400
How dare you?

99
00:09:20,233 --> 00:09:23,366
I thought I finally found my safe zone.

100
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:27,600
But clearly, I didn't.

101
00:09:29,133 --> 00:09:30,433
Claire, please listen.

102
00:09:30,766 --> 00:09:31,233
No.

103
00:09:32,366 --> 00:09:37,300
To you, I'm just a fictional character you use for your writing.

104
00:09:40,200 --> 00:09:42,033
But I'm sorry to say

105
00:09:42,033 --> 00:09:44,066
This novel has come to an end.

106
00:09:45,533 --> 00:09:48,166
Go back and write your perfect ending...

107
00:09:48,166 --> 00:09:50,166
in your own fantasy world.

108
00:09:59,266 --> 00:10:01,500
You made everything we had...

109
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Feel like it was just your job.

110
00:10:06,933 --> 00:10:09,000
It wasn't all like that, Claire.

111
00:10:09,933 --> 00:10:12,500
I started this because of work, yes.

112
00:10:13,133 --> 00:10:16,000
But then things got out of my control.

113
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:21,000
My feelings for you are completely real.

114
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Real?

115
00:10:22,433 --> 00:10:23,433
You're a writer.

116
00:10:23,433 --> 00:10:26,500
You can't even tell truth from fiction, can you?

117
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:30,500
Even when we looked at each other...

118
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:32,500
You just saw me as words on a page.

119
00:10:33,366 --> 00:10:35,000
Claire, Eris is sorry.

120
00:10:36,766 --> 00:10:38,533
I admit it was really wrong of me...

121
00:10:38,533 --> 00:10:40,633
to profit off of your life.

122
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,800
But I'm not here for research.

123
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:47,233
I'm here to ask for another chance.

124
00:10:47,233 --> 00:10:48,266
Please, Claire.

125
00:10:55,766 --> 00:10:57,133
Save it for someone else.

126
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:11,200
Cher, I'm sorry.

127
00:11:16,866 --> 00:11:21,000
The person you should apologize to is Claire, not me.

128
00:11:23,766 --> 00:11:25,633
This whole mess is my fault.

129
00:11:26,733 --> 00:11:28,500
You should leave for today.

130
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:32,700
Let Claire cool down a bit, then you two can talk.

131
00:11:35,500 --> 00:11:36,266
Alright.

132
00:11:58,166 --> 00:12:01,000
What will you do about Ms. Eris?

133
00:12:01,300 --> 00:12:02,500
Do nothing.

134
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:04,800
Hey, be serious.

135
00:12:05,300 --> 00:12:08,000
I really don't think she meant it.

136
00:12:08,266 --> 00:12:09,800
From what I know about her...

137
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:11,000
She seems like a good person.

138
00:12:12,200 --> 00:12:14,533
Honestly, you know her better than I do.

139
00:12:15,366 --> 00:12:17,633
Do you really think she did this on purpose?

140
00:12:18,533 --> 00:12:20,000
Think about it carefully.

141
00:12:27,933 --> 00:12:28,933
Claire.

142
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:33,000
I have nothing to say to you.

143
00:12:33,866 --> 00:12:35,200
Wait a second, Claire.

144
00:12:37,366 --> 00:12:40,500
This is the cancellation contract for the novel.

145
00:12:40,733 --> 00:12:42,700
I'll delete the entire manuscript.

146
00:12:42,700 --> 00:12:45,800
Even if it bankrupts me in fines, I don't care.

147
00:12:45,800 --> 00:12:48,066
But Claire, I want you to know.

148
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:50,700
You're not just a generic plot.

149
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:54,000
You're the person I truly want a happy ending with.

150
00:12:56,533 --> 00:12:57,500
So what?

151
00:13:02,133 --> 00:13:05,000
This is the only copy in the world written just for you.

152
00:13:05,766 --> 00:13:07,400
I've deleted all the files.

153
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:10,000
And these are my genuine feeling.

154
00:13:11,933 --> 00:13:15,166
Chapter One: Claire is not a character.

155
00:13:15,166 --> 00:13:17,166
But the one who taught me that

156
00:13:17,166 --> 00:13:20,133
my heart to race whenever she's near.

157
00:13:20,766 --> 00:13:24,033
Chapter Two: The scent of dogs on Claire

158
00:13:24,033 --> 00:13:25,733
smells better than any expensive perfume

159
00:13:25,733 --> 00:13:26,833
I've ever encountered.

160
00:13:30,066 --> 00:13:31,200
Nonsense.

161
00:13:32,333 --> 00:13:35,466
And the final chapter, Special Chapter.

162
00:13:35,466 --> 00:13:38,500
This writer promises to take care of you for the rest of her life.

163
00:13:38,933 --> 00:13:42,000
Let this story belong only to Claire and to us.

164
00:13:42,766 --> 00:13:45,800
I made this to apologize for everything I did.

165
00:13:46,600 --> 00:13:48,300
I know what I did was wrong.

166
00:13:49,933 --> 00:13:51,200
I'm so sorry.

167
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:05,600
One

168
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:06,633
Two

169
00:14:06,633 --> 00:14:07,566
Three

170
00:14:08,233 --> 00:14:09,233
Four

171
00:14:09,266 --> 00:14:10,400
Five

172
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:11,400
Six

173
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:12,333
Seven

174
00:14:21,766 --> 00:14:25,666
I don't know why, but when I'm upset...

175
00:14:25,666 --> 00:14:28,533
The only place I feel safe being weak...

176
00:14:28,533 --> 00:14:30,266
Is right here with you, Claire.

177
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:36,000
I think I starting to like you.

178
00:14:37,166 --> 00:14:38,800
I like you too.

179
00:14:44,266 --> 00:14:46,800
My feelings for you are completely real.

180
00:14:49,733 --> 00:14:51,000
Please forgive me.

181
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:52,600
Claire.

182
00:15:11,366 --> 00:15:12,600
You weirdo.

183
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:18,500
In the end, love isn't like a novel.

184
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:22,066
It's about letting down your guard and being real with each other.

185
00:16:25,500 --> 00:16:28,166
We might fall sometimes,

186
00:16:28,733 --> 00:16:33,033
but as long as we learn

187
00:16:33,033 --> 00:16:35,100
and write the next chapter together,

188
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:38,366
that's all that matters.

189
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,133
Excuse me, is this Love Lab?

190
00:17:32,366 --> 00:17:33,500
Yes, it is.

191
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,500
The shop is so pretty. Just like the owner.

192
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:42,200
Thank you.

193
00:17:43,466 --> 00:17:48,000
How can I help you today?

194
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:51,800
Do you have a girlfriend service?

195
00:17:54,900 --> 00:18:00,500
Well, you'll have to try the service first to see if you like it.

196
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:03,900
If you do, we can talk.

197
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:09,433
Would you like to try it right now?
